Cell[TextData[{
 "Then I would think about what I actually wanted to come out of the \
function.  For instance:\n1) Do I want to know how long it took to make the \
loop?\n2) Do I want to know the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]x\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]y\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]z\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] values or just the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]y\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]z\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]?\n3) Do I want vector output?\n4) Do I want to \
compute the sensitivity as I go round the loop?\n5) \[Ellipsis]\nI guess the \
first thing I should do is make one that just returns the new point on the \
surface.  It takes in a vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"y", ",", "z"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
